        "proposal_id": "P0000",
        "source_refs": [
          "F000:F006"
        ],
        "rationale": "F000 permits a covered entity to require an employment entrance medical examination and condition an offer of employment on its results after an offer is made and prior to the commencement of duties, subject to statutory conditions. F001, F002, and F006 set forth conditions (A), (B), and (C) connected conjunctively by 'and', while F003 through F005 set forth the confidentiality exceptions (i), (ii), and (iii). P0000 accurately preserves the conjunctive requirement that all three conditions must be satisfied and faithfully captures the scope of the confidentiality exceptions.",
        "verdict": "supported"
      },
      {
        "proposal_id": "P0001",
        "source_refs": [
          "F000:F006"
        ],
        "rationale": "F000 through F006 structure the prerequisites for requiring an employment entrance examination as cumulative conditions joined by 'and' before subparagraph (C). P0001 incorrectly characterizes these conditions as disjunctive alternatives ('provided any one of these three alternative conditions is met... or...'), which would erroneously allow an employer to satisfy only one requirement (such as using results in accordance with the subchapter) while disregarding the requirement that all entering employees be examined regardless of disability or that records be kept confidential.",
        "verdict": "unsupported"
      }
    ]
  }
